  <p style="margin-top:var(--space-10);max-width:var(--content-max);color:var(--text-2)">
    Four ideas run through every project below. First, build AI the way you build any software - 
    with clear structure and tested parts. Second, check that the system actually does what it claims.
    Third, question the model itself and how you measure it. Fourth, question the machines it runs on.
    Every model has a cutoff point for when it is sure enough. Where you set that cutoff is a
    <strong>business decision, not a technical one</strong>. Sending a support ticket to the wrong team
    costs ten minutes. Missing a line in a patient's file costs far more. Every project below answers
    the same question: <strong>which mistake can we afford?</strong></p>

